    "rationale": "Iteration 8 (kp 2.2, kd 0.3, ki 0, base_speed 1.1 on the iteration 5 and 7 geometry) is the best result so far at 88.24. Its S-bend and slalom line-loss events fell from 1.0 to 0.05 each, and oval line loss stayed at 0. Max_error is still 0.061 to 0.062 m, just above the fixed 0.06 m limit, and no run finishes. The Builder's geometry is held exactly as in iterations 5, 7 and 8, so the controller is the only variable I can change. Geometry follows the Builder's proposal: seven 16 mm sensors at x = -0.05 to +0.05 m, y = 0.04 m, body 0.18 x 0.12 m, mass 0.6 kg, wheel_track 0.10 m, wheel_radius 0.03 m. Iteration 8 shows that the controller now drives most of the line-loss gain. The remaining question is whether more damping at bend onset reduces max_error further. Iteration 1 showed that kp 3.0 raised oscillation, and iteration 8 showed that kp 2.2 with kd 0.3 reduced line loss, so I keep kp at 2.2 and raise kd modestly from 0.3 to 0.35 to damp the overshoot. Base_speed stays at 1.1 and ki stays at 0, because the integral has not helped and adds windup on curves. Expected result: S-bend and slalom line loss stays at or near 0, and max_error trends below the 0.06 m limit. If kd 0.35 is worse than iteration 8, the next package should return to kd 0.3. Score is expected near 88, with a risk of a small drop.",
