  "entityR1": {
    "feedback": "Written before this candidate has raced. Iteration 8 (kp 2.2, kd 0.3, ki 0, base_speed 1.1 on the iteration 5 and 7 geometry) is the best so far at 88.24. It cut S-bend and slalom line loss from 1.0 to 0.05 each and left oval line loss at 0. This supports the controller-side view: lowering kp and raising damping at bend onset helped, while earlier speed cuts (iteration 5) and kp increases (iteration 1, iteration 7) did not. The Integrator's package keeps your geometry and tests a modest kd rise to 0.35. Decide the next geometry from the next race as follows. If S-bend and slalom line_loss_events are still 0.05 or more with geometry fixed, the loss is not geometric, so do not edit geometry; ask the Integrator where on the course it starts. If line_loss_events is 0 on all three tracks but max_error still approaches 0.06 m, the bend turn authority is the limit, so widen wheel_track to 0.12 m. This is the only change that addresses the max_error limit, since body_width cannot move it (max(0.06, 0.0125 + body_width/4) stays at 0.06 m for body_width up to 0.18 m). If the robot completes and completion_time exceeds 2.5 s, test wheel_radius 0.035 m. Progress is still 0.12 to 0.33, so runs must first reach the finish before top speed matters.",
